#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# The whole site. Owns the transport and nothing else: each domain is detached
# and brings its own routes, so this file never learns what a thread or a board
# is.
#
# Order matters twice over.
#
# The LANDING PAGE is added first. HttpServer::ResolvePath walks typed children
# in the order they were added and takes the first match, so a page a lobby
# script attached could otherwise answer "/" too. Adding landing here, before
# any lobby is detached, is what makes that deterministic rather than a
# function of which script ran first. (chess_web.etcs attaches no pages now:
# only the /game route.)
#
# The lobbies are detached AFTER Start, and what makes them find THIS server
# rather than minting a second one that cannot bind 8080 is the verb their own
# web scripts use: `ensure NetworkProvider::HttpServer web`
# (NetworkProvider/scripts/chess_web.etcs). `ensure` takes the name if it
# already resolves and spawns only if it does not; `spawn` ALWAYS creates and
# refuses a name that already resolves (spawn_entity, core/CommandExecutor.h),
# so a subscript that spells it `spawn` fails in exactly the session it was
# written for.
#
# Their own Start calls are no-ops: StartConcrete returns false when a manager
# already exists. Their duplicate FileHtmlPage children are harmless for the
# same first-match reason, just redundant.

spawn NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8080)

# Cross-origin isolation, site-wide, which is what makes SharedArrayBuffer --
# and therefore threads -- available at all. /paint is a -pthread wasm build and
# its Workers die on `wasmMemory is undefined` without these two; the same pair
# serve_paint.etcs already carries, moved up here because AddHeader is a property
# of the SERVER and there is one server.
#
# Safe for the pages that came first, and checked rather than assumed: every
# cross-origin url anywhere in www/ is an <a href> (github, youtube,
# anticurrententropy.com), and COEP governs SUBRESOURCES, not navigation. The
# one behaviour this does change is that a link opened in a new tab loses
# window.opener -- which nothing here reads.
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy same-origin)
web.AddHeader(Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy require-corp)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::StaticHtmlPage landing)
landing.SetHtmlFromFile(ACE_ROOT/scripts/www/index.html)

# Everything else is disk layout as url layout: /whitepaper.html,
# /philosophy.html. One page type, no per-document entity, and adding a
# document is copying a file rather than editing this script. A page that is a
# module's front (the forum, server-played chess) is mounted from the module
# (site_pages.etcs) rather than copied here.
web.spawn(NetworkProvider::FileHtmlPage tree)
# THE LINK HUB, for a shared canvas and for a game of chess. A page hosts a
# Room in its own runtime through this hub (PaintShare, paint_host.etcs;
# ChessShare, chess_host.etcs), and the people it invites link to it here at
# /link/<session>: the hub splices bytes between them and holds nothing of
# the session. The chess hall and the ranked tables are Rooms of this
# runtime's own on the same hub (/link/hall, /link/table1).
web.spawn(NetworkProvider::LinkHub links)
tree.LoadFromDisk(ACE_ROOT/scripts/www)
run site_pages.etcs tree=tree
# The pages link without the extension (/chess/'s "/chess-classic"), as the
# TLS spelling of this site already answers.
tree.SetDefaultExtension(.html)
tree.ListPaths()

# ── the wasm apps ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Each a self-contained site under a prefix of its own, from its module's own
# list of files, and the runtime they share at /wasm/ (site_apps.etcs).
run site_apps.etcs tree=tree

# Printed again after the app mounts, not only after LoadFromDisk: this is the
# fastest way to catch a staging mistake, and every name added above is one the
# page will ask for.
tree.ListPaths()

# The tar-pit: a self-registering, gate-level filter that catches
# bot-scan-shaped paths (.env, wp-admin, .php, ...) and answers them with a
# deliberately slow 404 instead of routing them anywhere real -- see
# TarpitNode.h for why it lives here as its own entity rather than a flag on
# HttpServer or ConnectionManager.
spawn NetworkProvider::TarpitNode tarpit
tarpit.LoadDefaultTarpitPatterns()

# AddHandler @tarpit Request @tarpit Filter registers the tar-pit as a
# FILTERED gate-level consumer -- ConnectionManager::dispatchToSubscribers
# tries every filtered subscriber before falling back to unfiltered ones, so
# a scan-shaped path is caught here and never reaches web's own Serve.
#
# AddHandler @web Serve is NOT redundant with what Start does automatically
# -- it looks identical to the implicit default (StartConcrete registers
# web's own Serve when handlers_ is empty), but the moment ANY handler is
# added, handlers_ stops being empty and that implicit default is skipped.
# Without this second line, the tar-pit would be the ONLY registered
# consumer and every real request would find no unfiltered fallback and be
# dropped. Declaring it explicitly here is what keeps that fallback alive
# now that a filtered handler exists at all.
web.AddHandler(@tarpit Request @tarpit Filter)
web.AddHandler(@web Serve)

web.Start()
web.IsStarted()

# THE HALL AND THE RANKED TABLES, on the hub above: the name server every
# casual game finds its partner through, and the two tables this runtime
# hosts and judges (ChessProvider/scripts/chess_service.etcs).
run ChessProvider/scripts/chess_service.etcs links=links
detach forum_lobby.etcs


# http://localhost:8080/